-- `Reject.FixedArray.yana`'s last case on its own: the new stage stops at a declaration
-- error, so beside the body rules it hid all of them.

{-
   A fixed array of itself has no finite size, and there is no edge to cut.

   `breakLayoutCycles` inserts an indirection at the back edge of a record cycle; a fixed array has
   none to insert one on - boxing the element would make `[Cell *4]` four pointers, which is a
   different type from the one that was written. So this is reported instead of silently becoming
   something else.
-}
data Cell {kids: [Cell *4]}

fn main() -> Int = 0
